Z||000006||Monkeyman||06-02-2000||10:01 AM||||I'm not a huge fan of leather seats, but BENGAL4 has a set in his GT and they look great.  I think they're Mr. Mikes, but I could be wrong.  If I were going to do leather, I'd go for Mr. Mikes in a heartbeat.  I had planned on putting a set of seats in from a Cav Z24, but the guy with them (former member) hasn't sent them and won't return my phone calls.  If I can't get these seats from him, I might try to find some F-body seats.  Someone bought a pair for $100 I think.  Maybe if I wait long enough I'll be able to find the same deal. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||06-02-2000||12:03 PM||||Shiner, I know a few people in our local club who have had Mr. Mikes seats for a few years and it is their daily driver. The seats hold up very well. They use "mink oil" to keep the seats from cracking in the winter time. The mink oil also keeps them soft and new looking!||||reg||1
Z||000008||frontal lobe||06-02-2000||12:20 PM||||Congratulations!!  Your wife may not care, but we do.  Hey, at least she let you spend it on leather seats instead of, say, new patio furniture.<P>Oreif, does mink oil rub off on your pants?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fret Naught||06-07-2000||03:37 PM||||Finally got hold of Mike of Mr. Mike's on Friday, he would not start my seats until I got leather samples to choose from, they got here on Monday, man that was quick (he is in Fl. and I am in WA.) any way chose my leather and placed the order yesterday should get them in a couple of weeks. Can't wait. Mr. Mike seemed real concerned that I get just what I wanted real service oriented, I think I will like doing business with him. The only concern I have is that part of the seat is Vinyl, I hope it doesn't look tacky.||||reg||1
Z||000010||bHooper||06-07-2000||04:07 PM||||typically, most leather furniture and seat's have leather on the portions that make contact with the body, and use vinyl on the rear and sides.  generally, it doesnt look all that bad.<P>i am interested in useing mr mikes, when i do my interior.  he also offers leather covered door panels, and i believe... recovered/s the center console!<P>but for now, i must make do.<P><B>fret</B>, what color/condition are your current seats?  i could use a grey factory seat cover (w/o rips).<P>let me know.<P>hoop||||reg||1
