Z||000018||Oreif||06-08-2000||02:38 AM||||No the mink oil does not rub off the seats. It's more like a creamy paste. You rub it in and buff it out simular to waxing a car. No oily or greasy film. It's not like using armor-all where the seats get slick and slimy.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Monkeyman||06-08-2000||02:49 PM||||If you ever feel like you must use Armor-All on your car, <B>DO NOT</B> use it on the seats, steering wheel or pedals!!!!!!  I used to own an award winning truck.  One of my ex wives decided to use that nasty stuff on all of the above (leather seats, leather wrapped steering wheel, polished aluminum pedals).  I spent 3 hours trying to wipe the stuff off and still couldn't stay in the seat, steer or keep my feet on the pedals for a couple of days!  ||||reg||1
Z||000020||olympic||06-08-2000||03:04 PM||||  Many years ago a friend of mine bought an old Dodge Duster with vinyl bench seats.  He thought it would be a good idea to armor-all the seats.  Well, it was the funniest thing I ever saw.  It was almost impossible to drive the car.  Every time he would turn a corner or hit the brakes, you would have to hold onto the dash or door handles because you would slide all over the place!!||||reg||1
